WEBVTT

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.880
"January 30th, 1961
Local Time - 0:05 PM"

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.970
"January 30th, 1961
Local Time - 0:05 PM"
On January 30th, 1961,
the UK sent a chimpanzee into space

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:26.060
as part of Project Hermes,
their manned spaceflight program.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:31.400
Though nearly dying due to
equipment failure, it safely returned.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.700
The chimpanzee was named Sam
and quickly became famous.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:43.620
Unbelievable! At this rate,
we'll be passed up by the UK!

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.620
"1st Design Bureau - Chief's Office"
My apologies. We're currently working
on improvements to the cabin

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.090
to fix the issues which
occurred on N44's flight.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.300
Yes.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.800
Yes.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.520
Absolutely. By spring, as planned.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.900
Good. I'm counting on you, Comrade Chief.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.440
You're too worked up over a little monkey.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.150
I won't be beat by those hamburger lovers!

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:22.410
Still, it's a problem if our
cosmonauts don't come home alive.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:27.250
Our Mechta Shest...
I can't wait to see who's chosen.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.890
Good morning, Lev.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:03.410
"Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut"

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:18.360
"The White Rose of Sangrad"

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.490
"January 31st - 11:30 AM"
As for the results of the graduation test:

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:24.450
"Training Center - Conference Room"
These top three Mechta Shest
will be selected as cosmonauts

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.910
with the other three as reserves.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.920
Private Mikhail Yashin.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.830
Sir!

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:36.170
Private Roza Plevitskaya.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.130
Sir!

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.880
Finally, the last of the three.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.010
Private Lev Leps.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.970
Huh? Uh... Sir!

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.610
And now for the reserves:
Private Semyon Adamov.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.860
Sir!

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.280
Private Stepan Levitzky.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.070
Sir!

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.200
--I was chosen...!
--Private Zhores Rimsky.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.990
--I'm going to space!
--Sir!

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.330
Mikhail! Roza! Congratulations!

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:17.920
Only the first cosmonaut will be
remembered. The others, not so much.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:24.970
I know that, but we're comrades in
the race to space, and I'm proud of that.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:29.310
Apparently, the brass
values that view of yours.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:33.230
But your tongue is honey
and your heart is ice.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.060
Uh...

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.900
So, congrats. Hmph!

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.150
See you, Lev.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:49.200
Whatever. I am who I am.
Oh, right! I'll let her know!

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.870
Yeah?

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:58.130
Huh? I was picked as a cosmonaut,
just like I promised!

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.380
You're not excited?

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:08.260
You weren't picked to fly first yet,
right? And, third! You barely made it in!

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.470
Oh, Irinyan!

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:14.930
She says that, but she was
dying to know the results!

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:20.070
What's more, she threw a pine cone
into the lake and prayed for you--!

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:21.150
Anya!

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.530
Pine cone?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:26.400
I-It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:32.240
Hey! What's that face supposed to--?!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:49.890
Don't laugh! You could be
the world's first cosmonaut!

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:52.640
No, the world's first cosmonaut is--

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.680
Don't you dare lose to another human.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.850
I'll suck out your blood
and make you a mummy!

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.650
I'll do my best.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.150
You better!

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.320
"The Makings of a Cosmonaut"

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:14.120
"February 1st - 3:20 PM"

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:14.740
"February 1st - 3:20 PM"
A sudden stop at 100 kilometers an hour?

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:20.330
"Rocket Sled - Deceleration Training"
N44 passed out just before
she entered zero-G.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:25.050
"Biomedical Lab
Vice-Director Pavlov"
But for the real flight,
we need you conscious at all times.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:35.350
We'll have you sit in this special device
to experience drastic deceleration.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.810
Insane.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:42.020
Don't worry. Our tests already
demonstrated that it's safe.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.860
So, who wants to be first?

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.490
Me! I'll do it!

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:58.370
"February 7th - 10:21 AM"

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.330
"Drop Tower - Zero-G Training"

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:10.090
With the data gained by N44
and the Nosferatu Project's success,

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:14.260
training was adapted
to incorporate what was learned.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.680
"February 16th - 9:30 AM"

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.690
"Training Center - Centrifuge Training"

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.150
"Training Center - Centrifuge Training"
If Irina handled this, I can, too!

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:29.320
I promised her that I'd go to space!

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.910
Irinyan! Irinyan!

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.870
I knocked, but...

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:43.790
I come bearing the latest news
from the training center!

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:47.960
No surprise, the top candidate
is Comrade Yashin.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:53.720
He has high social standing,
high scores, and he's handsome!

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:58.680
Next is the White Rose of Sangrad,
Comrade Plevitskaya!

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.600
You already know all about her.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:08.940
The White Rose of Sangrad... Her?
Though, I can't deny she's full of thorns.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:13.450
Still, the fact she's a woman
is causing a stir.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.320
Is that bad?

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:20.830
The UZSR claims both genders are equal,
but her chances are slim.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:23.620
So, what are Lev's chances?

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:27.170
Oh? Curious about him, are we?

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:34.180
Good grief! You don't have to run away!

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.180
I'm just going for a walk!

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.220
In that outfit?

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.640
Something wrong?

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.480
N-No.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:48.020
Hey, Anya.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:51.320
I've proven useful, right?

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.650
Huh?

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:58.780
The things you've learned from
my body have been helpful, right?

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:03.580
I still have value, don't I?

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:09.250
Of course! Thanks to you,
the ship is being improved!

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.630
And their training, too!

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.210
Let's hope so.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.010
It's okay, Irinyan.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.270
It'll all be okay.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:40.200
"A Thorny Passion"

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.580
"February 21st - 0:10 PM"

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:44.330
"Dormitory - Cafeteria"

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:55.420
Eating in the suit makes it all seem
so real. We're even training in the cabin.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.550
You think?

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:01.010
Yeah! Doesn't the thought
of going to space excite you?

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:04.060
What makes you think you'll be flying?

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:07.690
Jeez. Your attitude's something else.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.450
See you in the drop zone!

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:15.840
Good!

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:22.890
Shoot!

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:48.120
It's not serious. It shouldn't
impact your training.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.370
"Training Center - Exam Room"
However, I'm advising three days of rest.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:54.750
You sure get hurt a lot, don't you?

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:55.960
Sorry.

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.960
Hey, Lev!

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.130
Trying to get yourself killed?!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:05.680
...is what I'd like to say,
but I'll let it slide this time.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:12.020
Well done, Lev. You risked peril to save
a comrade. That's what soldiers do.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:13.400
Thank you.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.480
Mmm.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:19.190
Um... And how is Roza?

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.990
We're lucky no one was hurt.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:30.410
And we get three days off?
Everyone will be envious.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:31.450
Yeah.

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.790
Why... did you save me?

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:44.680
Why? When a pal's about to die in front
of you, you don't really think about it.

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:49.470
A pal, huh?

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:54.100
Your tongue is honey...
and your heart is ice.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:13:01.860
Correction: Your heart is honey, too.
Enough to pair it with sugar and jam.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.530
Ugh. Talk about heartburn.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:11.040
Hey, lemme grab a drink.

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:14.330
Huh?

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.330
My treat. Shall we sit down?

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:26.340
I'm out of the running.

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:27.390
Huh?

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:33.180
If you hadn't saved me,
I probably would've died.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:37.310
My body wouldn't move.
I thought it was over.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:48.240
When I joined the Air Force, I was looked
down upon for being a woman.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:52.490
That's why I refused to lose to anyone.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:57.290
I crushed everyone who
made fun of me in dogfights.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:04.340
After doing it long enough, I was called
"The White Rose of Sangrad."

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.300
But...

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:12.140
There's nothing beautiful about me.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:20.020
I've been pushing so hard since
becoming a final candidate.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:24.320
I knew I had to completely
outscore you and Mikhail.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:27.950
Otherwise, they'd never
pick a woman to fly first.

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:32.950
I don't think gender matters much
when it comes to space.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.910
You're the only one who thinks that.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:51.510
I hate to admit it,
but you're stronger than me.

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:56.850
Both emotionally and physically.
And today proved that.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:58.600
That's not true.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:04.360
I didn't want to lose,
no matter what it took.

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:09.530
By attacking others,
I felt like I was protecting myself.

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:15.660
There's no beautiful bloom,
just a thorny vine. That's me.

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.540
Lev Leps.

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:25.050
I apologize for my behavior.
I'm sorry for the things I've said.

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:27.590
Y-Yeah.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:30.130
To her, too.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.260
Oh, Irina?

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:37.060
Yes. I don't know why
I said those nasty things to her.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:41.560
She endured the training
and returned from space.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:44.810
N44 is an incredible cosmonaut.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.650
It's Irina. Irina Luminesk.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:53.450
Irina... That's right.
She has a name, too.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:59.250
The experimental subject...
The vampire that beat humans to space.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.420
Where is she now?

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:17.260
Was she disposed of?

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.310
No.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:23.650
She can't be. That would be injustice.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.610
What's wrong, Irinyan?

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:33.030
Changed my mind.
Forget soda water, let's go shopping.

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:34.860
Eh?

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:41.580
It's unusual for you to wanna
come shopping here.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:47.090
I'm not a shut-in all the time.
And I won't be able to come here soon.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.300
Well...

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:54.260
Irinyan, what will you tell Lev?

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:56.970
The same thing they told me.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:59.350
But, that's...

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:01.850
It doesn't concern Lev.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:05.150
That's right--no matter what I do.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:17.120
Irinyan!

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.580
Irinyan!

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:20.990
Hey! What was that?!

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.120
Are you two okay?

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.830
Natalia...?

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.880
"February 22nd - 1:53 AM"

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:38.390
"Underground Base"
Wait! Why?! I was just getting rid
of the vampire for our motherland!

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:43.770
We're an organization. We mustn't
act without orders from above.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:48.440
B-But as long as she lives,
there's a threat of our secrets leaking--!

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:55.240
"That's News to Me"

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:58.370
"February 27th - 5:10 PM"

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:01.120
--He's late!
--He'll be here soon.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:05.160
I thought soldiers were
supposed to be punctual.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:12.050
Huh? What?

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:14.420
You protected her and got hurt?

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:19.340
Yeah, but it's nothing serious.
See? I'm fine!

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.890
Long time no see, Lev.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:29.560
Yeah. With all the training, I haven't
had a chance to come for like a month.

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.900
Is that why you're mad?

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:36.740
No. I'm sure our future
"hero" is a busy guy.

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:41.370
Your hands are full drinking
soda water with your comrades.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:46.910
Soda water? True, we're banned
from drinking alcohol for now, but...

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:53.460
Hmm? That's all you wanted to tell me?

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:56.630
Uh, no... Not exactly...

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.170
Then what?

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.970
I'm leaving this city.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.180
Eh?

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:06.680
I'm transferring--leaving here
and going to Sangrad.

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:11.770
I'll undergo health exams while
working at the Design Bureau.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.650
Are you serious?

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.070
Yeah. Got a problem?

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:18.860
Comrade Chief insisted upon it.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:25.990
Irina is a quick learner and he thinks
her flight experience might be invaluable.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:29.500
I see. Well, that's a relief.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:32.710
Except she's supposed to start March 1st.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:34.670
Huh? That's in two days.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:37.630
Yeah, and I know tomorrow is sudden,

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:42.590
but how about a farewell party
for her and to wish you luck?

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:48.020
Sure, of course. Hmm?
Isn't tomorrow Armed Forces Day?

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:51.770
It's a national holiday,
so we'll all be off.

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:57.860
Yup! Let's play all day! Though in
our case, I suppose all night.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.610
Aren't you glad?

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:06.370
Go on, Irinyan.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:13.750
I-I don't need a farewell party,
but we should wish you luck.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:19.170
Don't get me wrong! I just don't
want some other human to win!

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:21.380
Thanks, Irina.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.010
It's settled, then!

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:32.020
But unfortunately, since I made
plans to go to Sangrad tomorrow,

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:34.060
it'll be just you two.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:35.110
--Eh?
--Huh?

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:38.320
Wh-What? That's news to me!

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:40.650
Huh? Didn't I mention it?

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:41.780
Anya!

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:47.530
And in this country, one mustn't
go back on their plans, right?

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:49.200
Y-Yeah.

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:01.300
So, tomorrow at six.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:06.550
Anya.

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:08.890
Yeah?

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:10.220
Thanks.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.850
"February 28th - Armed Forces Day"

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:22.650
Those two are such a handful.
Sometimes they need a push!

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:58.400
Right on time, huh?

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:50.970
"Next Episode:
'A Cold Spring'"
